          ],
          "DETECTOR": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": [
                "CEREN"
              ],
              "free_text": [
                " Gas Cherenkov Detector (GCD) with a response",
                "time of 7 ps when the energy threshold is set at 12",
                "MeV and variable energy thresholding capability to",
                "further reduce undesirable radiation backgrounds."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "SAMPLE": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": null,
              "free_text": [
                "The targets used were CH shells of approximately 1 mm",
                "diameter, between 14 microm to 20 microm wall",
                "thicknesses and filled with between 10 and 19",
                "atmospheres of equimolar DT fuel."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "METHOD": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": [
                "TOF"
              ],
              "free_text": [
                " To independently test the prediction for the DT",
                "gamma-ray spectrum, ICF experiments were performed",
                "using the Omega laser, which produced < 200 ps FWHM",
                "DT fusion source. The targets were imploded with 27",
                "kJ of 351 nm laser light using all 60 Omega beams.",
                "These targets produced fusion yields between 3*10**12",
                "and 3*10**13 total neutron output and ion",
                "temperatures between 3.5 keV to 5.5 keV. Difference",
                "in time-of-flight between fusion gamma-rays and",
                "neutrons allow for their temporal segregation at",
                "modest distances from the source, substantially",
                "avoiding the neutron-induced backgrounds, as compared",
                "to those observed in accelerator experiments. The",
                "desired gamma-ray signals were observed with a Gas",
                "Cherenkov Detector."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "ANALYSIS": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": null,
              "free_text": [
                "Comparison of the predicted gamma-ray spectrum to",
                "observation using a technique in which the spectrum",
                "is forward folded with a priori instrument response",
                "curves to create detector-responses as a function of",
                "threshold energy. These data were fitted to a third",
                "order polynomial weighted by errors using the IDL",
                "\"poly fit\" routine and yielded a reduced chi2 value",
                "of 0.63. By considering errors in the fit and",
                "variations between the ITS-ACCEPT and GEANT4 codes we",
                "measured the intensity ratio G1:G0 to be (2.1+-0.4):1."
              ]
            }
          ],
